librespot reconnects when its session to Spotify's servers is lost, and
`status` reports that session.

The session dies on a closed connection or a missed keep-alive and is
then invalid for good, but nothing acted on that while a Spirc stood:
its loop checks the session only when something wakes it, and with no
phone talking to the device that took minutes to hours here, with the
device advertised and playing nothing in between. The main loop now
retires the Spirc and connects again with the last credentials as soon
as the session is invalid, under the same rate limit as a Spirc that
shut itself down. `status` gains `session live|lost|none` so the app
can say when Spotify is unreachable rather than merely idle.

Applies on top of librespot-control-socket.patch.

